{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/591816-recs-for-world-war-cthulhu","id":591816,"title":"Recs for World War Cthulhu?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T14:43:47-07:00","id":591816,"title":"Recs for World War Cthulhu?","content":"The kickstarter for <b>World War Cthulhu: Cold War</b> ( <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/461807648/world-war-cthulhu-cold-war-for-the-call-of-cthulhu?ref=nav_search\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...ref=nav_search</a> ) is catching my eye. The whole concept - Cold War spy thriller meets H.P. Lovecraft - <i>is</i> tempting . . . <br /> <br /> However, I don't know &quot;Cubicle 7&quot;. Is anyone familiar with the first game in the series? <b>World War Cthulhu: Darkest Hour</b> (about World War II)? Strengths, weaknesses, cool ideas? I like the basic <b>Call of Cthulhu</b> game, but would like to know more before taking the plunge with the kickstarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:58:28-07:00","id":591875,"title":"","content":"I have not seen the other &quot;World War Cthulhu&quot; stuff, but Cubilcle 7 is the author of The Laundry RPG (the only one i have and have read) a modification of the CoC ruleset set in the Laundry-verse of Charles Stross and it is one of the best RPG's i have seen, they have good modifications on the mechanics and amazing fluff/game aids. The &quot;Monsters Manual&quot; equivalent &quot;they Mythos Dossiers&quot; Is my favorite all time RPG book as it is a bunch of things you can use as game aid's / handouts, fluff description of monsters, and then in the back, two pages of stat blocks for when you need them. The Players handbook (&quot;The Agents Handbook&quot;) ,is mostly description of how to do espionage with only a few extra rules. additionally, the art is on point as is the layout. <br /> <br /> For what it is worth, I have already backed this kick-starter because it looks awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}